{
 "id": "L9",
 "n": 9,
 "title": "Describing and comparing",
 "goal": "Describe people, places, colours and clothes, and compare things.",
 "notes": [
  {
   "h": "Describing a noun: a big house, a good person",
   "p": "To put a describing word in front of a noun, change its ending. {{커요}} (it's big) becomes {{큰}}: {{큰 집}}. After a final consonant add {{은}}: {{작아요}} becomes {{작은}}, {{좋아요}} becomes {{좋은}}. Words ending in {{해요}} become {{한}}: {{조용해요}} becomes {{조용한}}. Words built on {{있어요}} or {{없어요}} take {{는}}: {{맛있는}}, {{재미있는}}. Words that change ㅂ to {{워}} (like {{매워요}}, {{추워요}}) end in {{운}}: {{매운 음식}}.",
   "ex": [
    [
     "큰 집",
     "a big house"
    ],
    [
     "좋은 사람",
     "a good person"
    ],
    [
     "맛있는 음식",
     "delicious food"
    ],
    [
     "매운 음식",
     "spicy food"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Colours",
   "p": "Colour words end in {{색}} (colour): {{빨간색}}, {{파란색}}, {{검은색}}. Right before a noun you can drop {{색}}: {{빨간 차}}. When the colour stands alone, as in asking for one, keep {{색}}: {{검은색 주세요}}.",
   "ex": [
    [
     "빨간 차",
     "a red car"
    ],
    [
     "검은색 주세요",
     "The black one, please."
    ],
    [
     "무슨 색 좋아해요?",
     "What colour do you like?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Three verbs for \"wear\"",
   "p": "English uses \"wear\" for everything; Korean picks the verb by what you put on. {{입어요}} for clothes on your body, {{신어요}} for shoes and socks, {{써요}} for hats and glasses. These verbs mean \"put on\", so \"is wearing\" is {{-고 있어요}}: {{모자를 쓰고 있어요}}.",
   "ex": [
    [
     "옷을 입어요",
     "I put on clothes."
    ],
    [
     "신발을 신어요",
     "I put on my shoes."
    ],
    [
     "안경을 써요",
     "I wear glasses."
    ],
    [
     "모자를 쓰고 있어요",
     "I'm wearing a hat."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Comparing: than, more, the most, the same, like",
   "p": "{{보다}} means \"than\" and goes right after the thing you compare against: {{이게 저거보다 더 싸요}} = this one is cheaper than that one. {{더}} = more, {{제일}} = the most. {{같아요}} = it's the same, {{달라요}} = it's different. {{처럼}} = like, in the same way as.",
   "ex": [
    [
     "오늘은 어제보다 더 추워요.",
     "It's colder today than yesterday."
    ],
    [
     "여기 뭐가 제일 맛있어요?",
     "What's the most delicious thing here?"
    ],
    [
     "한국 사람처럼 말하고 싶어요.",
     "I want to speak like a Korean."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Sounds: silent ㅎ, sliding letters, double final consonants",
   "p": "{{같아요}} is said {{가타요}}: the final ㅌ slides into the next syllable. ㅎ goes silent between sounds: {{좋은}} sounds like {{조은}}, and {{많이}} like {{마니}}. Before ㄴ, the ㅆ in {{있}} turns into ㄴ: {{맛있는}} is said {{마신는}}. With two final letters, the second slides over: {{짧아요}} is said {{짤바요}}, {{넓어요}} is said {{널버요}}.",
   "ex": [
    [
     "같아요",
     "It's the same."
    ],
    [
     "좋은 사람",
     "a good person"
    ],
    [
     "머리가 짧아요",
     "She has short hair."
    ]
   ]
  }
 ],
